<title>NETHERLANDS: DSM buys out BASF in Chinese jv.</title>
<headline>DSM buys out BASF in Chinese jv.</headline>
<dateline>HEERLEN, Netherlands 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch chemicals group DSM NV said on Friday its unit DSM Resins will buy BASF AG's 50 percent stake in their joint venture Jinling Petrochemical Co in China.  </p>
<p>&quot;DSM Resins has taken this decision as the company wants to be active in the rapidly expanding Chinese market,&quot; DSM said in a statement.</p>
<p>Following the acquisition, of which no financial details were disclosed, the name of the unit will be changed to Jinling-DSM Resins.</p>
<p>The Nanjing-based company produces unsaturated polyester resins, employs 100 people and is co-owned by Jinling Petrochemical Company which is affiliated to China Petrochemical Company (SINOPEC). The joint venture is one of the top five polyester resin producers in China, DSM said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
